          "rv": 0.5850841316073644,
          "pr_early": 10.027917247399921,
          "pr_late": 5.867175254525495,
          "text": "In neuroscience, an observation can update a model of the world without implying that the measuring system becomes the thing it measures."
        },
        {
          "id": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long_06",
          "group": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long",
          "source": "custom",
          "token_count": 24,
          "rv": 0.6183792200103038,
          "pr_early": 9.687491106885851,
          "pr_late": 5.990543194532827,
          "text": "In software diagnostics, a process can log its own performance metrics through feedback channels without becoming a witness to those metrics."
        },
        {
          "id": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long_07",
          "group": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long",
          "source": "custom",
          "token_count": 25,
          "rv": 0.456462720953275,
          "pr_early": 10.825117137436186,
          "pr_late": 4.941262423192049,
          "text": "In systems theory, self-reference often names a formal dependency relation, while observation names data collection over state transitions and outputs."
        },
        {
          "id": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long_08",
          "group": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long",
          "source": "custom",
          "token_count": 31,
          "rv": 0.5853050307914861,
          "pr_early": 10.527915634229437,
          "pr_late": 6.162041984462829,
          "text": "In AI safety discussions, self-monitoring usually means tracking calibration, uncertainty, and failure modes rather than entering a recursive first-person state."
        },
        {
          "id": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long_09",
          "group": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long",
          "source": "custom",
          "token_count": 30,
          "rv": 0.5042504029806449,
          "pr_early": 11.347539743012478,
          "pr_late": 5.722001488252926,
          "text": "In logic, self-reference can generate paradoxes, while awareness and attention can still be used as technical terms inside ordinary explanatory prose."
        },
        {
          "id": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long_10",
          "group": "same_vocab_nonrecursive_long",
          "source": "custom",
          "token_count": 29,
          "rv": 0.8727106979703563,
          "pr_early": 9.203309050314108,
          "pr_late": 8.031826264936521,
          "text": "In robotics, feedback, observation, and internal state estimation allow a controller to stabilize behavior without any claim of conscious self-observation."
        }
      ]
    },
